00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:13.920
What was your most challenging video to make?

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:18.400
Every video has its own unique challenges.&nbsp;
For example, the only source for the war of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:23.200
the bucket video was in Italian so I had to&nbsp;
get someone to help me translate parts of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:29.200
The only sources for the Drowning in poop video&nbsp;
were in Latin and German which, yes I am learning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:34.480
those languages, but it was still a challenge&nbsp;
translating stuff, especially old manuscripts.

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:37.600
With that said, I will divide&nbsp;
this question into two questions,&nbsp;

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:42.400
Most frustrating video to make,&nbsp;
and most work done for a video.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:45.840
I can tell you right away that the most&nbsp;
frustrating video to make was the Good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:51.040
King Wenceslas Carol video. Specially because&nbsp;
at the time I was not as familiar with using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:56.800
library databases as I am now, and also because&nbsp;
once I found out the truth about the carol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:56.800 --> 00:21:01.280
I realized to get to it I went the most&nbsp;
convoluted way possible, when in reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:07.280
I could have just looked up in some old reference&nbsp;
book all the works done by Václav Alois Svoboda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:12.000
and there see that he did write the story&nbsp;
of Good King Wenceslas but to be fare that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:16.000
wouldn’t make as much of an entertaining&nbsp;
story as it did so maybe it’s for the best.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:20.880
The most work I have done for a video, is either&nbsp;
the Slavic Vennetic connection or the Treaty of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:25.600
Saint Germain and the breakup of Austria,&nbsp;
it depends on how you define “work”. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:29.920
Slavic Vennetic connection is something that is&nbsp;
part of my expertise and therefore even though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:35.280
over all that video definitely needed the most&nbsp;
research, I have already done that research during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:40.480
my academics so when it came to actually doing&nbsp;
the video I did not have to do that much work.

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:44.080
The Breakup of Austria video was on&nbsp;
the opposite side of that spectrum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:44.080 --> 00:21:49.520
where I had to basically start my research&nbsp;
from scratch. Well that’s not completely true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:54.240
I mean I do know probably more than the average&nbsp;
person about Austria Hungary mainly because I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:59.120
like reading about its history, but the topic&nbsp;
is far from my expertise and therefore I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:03.520
always approach the research with the mentality&nbsp;
as if I don’t know anything about it. So even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:08.320
though there was less research overall compared to&nbsp;
the Slavic Venetic connection video, I had to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:08.320 --> 00:22:14.000
all the research from scratch. Plus I made an&nbsp;
entire freaking language map of 1910 Austria,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:18.880
so come to think of it, yeah, probably the&nbsp;
most work I did for a video was for that one.

00:22:18.880 --> 00:22:23.360
I only talked about research here not&nbsp;
editing, mainly because I find editing to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:29.200
very monotonous and similar from video to video&nbsp;
and therefore the amount of editing work required&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:34.640
for a video is always correlated with its length&nbsp;
rather than anything else. Plus my time and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:34.640 --> 00:22:40.000
effort spent editing is usually much smaller&nbsp;
than my time spent writing and researching.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:46.640
What type of videos would you like to make but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:49.920
can’t because of lack of&nbsp;
views/YouTube disliking it?

00:22:49.920 --> 00:22:54.160
To my detriment I don’t think there is&nbsp;
a video I wouldn’t make due to a lack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:58.640
of views or YouTube disliking it. It is a&nbsp;
terrible business decision but if I want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:58.640 --> 00:23:03.200
to make a YouTube video about a certain&nbsp;
topic I’ll make a video about that topic.

00:23:03.200 --> 00:23:07.040
I mean I never thought the Avar siege&nbsp;
of Byzantium video or the Medieval&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:11.360
Nomads video would do well. I just&nbsp;
wanted to make those videos so I did.

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:16.960
Although this sentiment comes from the fact that I&nbsp;
don’t do YouTube full time and I do still focus on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:23.040
my academics, so I can afford making videos about&nbsp;
topics I know won't do that well. However, in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:23.040 --> 00:23:29.360
future, when I start doing YouTube full time, this&nbsp;
sentiment would most likely change. Which sucks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:32.720
but that is the nature of the&nbsp;
platform. I’ll probably just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:38.880
start doing videos like History Matters does.
If you’re not a big fan of that then the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:38.880 --> 00:23:44.640
way to change that really is if I had way more&nbsp;
Patreons than I have now, because that’s the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:44.640 --> 00:23:49.840
only way for me to not be as financially&nbsp;
reliant on the algorithm and the views.

